 "result": "The last commit (`df77eb8`, \"retry longer; lower tax on big orders\") changed two functions in two files.\n\n**1. `tax(price)` in `calc/pricing.py`**\n- **Before:** every price was taxed at `TAX_RATE`, which is 0.08 (8%).\n- **After:** prices under 1000 are still taxed at 8%. Prices of 1000 or more are taxed at 5%. The 0.05 is written directly into the function instead of being a named constant.\n- The cutoff is `price < 1000`, so a price of exactly 1000 already gets 5%. Because of this, tax goes down at the cutoff: a price of 999 is taxed 79.92, but 1000 is taxed only 50.00.\n\n**2. `backoff(attempt)` in `calc/upload.py`**\n- **Before:** the wait between upload retries was `2 ** attempt`, capped at 30.\n- **After:** the cap is now 60, so later retries can wait up to twice as long. Waits for attempts 0\u00e2\u20ac\u201c4 (1, 2, 4, 8, 16) are unchanged. Attempt 5 now waits 32 instead of 30, and attempt 6 or later waits 60. With the default of 7 retries (`MAX_UPLOAD_RETRIES`), the longest wait now hits the new 60 cap.\n\nThe commit changed nothing else. Neither file had other edits, and no tests were touched.",
